# Flow Studio Director

Read `skills/flow-studio-director/SKILL.md` in full before any video work.

Quick reference:
- Order is enforced by gates in `scripts/project_state.py`: script → cast →
  storyboard → (shots) → rough_cut → final. Only the user opens a gate
  (`--by user --note "<their words>"`). Characters are built and approved
  (`cast-set` with real files, `cast-approve`) before any keyframe or shot.
- Analyse the script first: `scripts/script_breakdown.py script.docx --out breakdown`
  + `references/script-analysis.md`; similar names are asked, never merged.
- Storyboard for sign-off before any video credit: `scripts/animatic.py`.
- Fix in post before regenerating: `scripts/edit_clip.py`; montage with
  transitions/J-L cuts: `scripts/assemble.py`; captions from the script,
  timed from the real clips: `scripts/captions.py`.
- After install or an ffmpeg update: `python3 skills/flow-studio-director/scripts/selftest.py`.
- Ask first (numbered options, one RECOMMENDED): platform, length, **model
  preference**, **autonomy mode** (guided / per_generation / per_shot
  default / autopilot with budget), dialogue language, budget.
- Price the plan: `python3 skills/flow-studio-director/scripts/shot_plan.py plan.json`
  (fix every ERROR). Read Flow's live cost before every generation.
- Route every shot individually (image first or not, frames vs
  ingredients, model, length) — `references/routing-principles.md`.
- On-screen dialogue is native to the video model with saved Flow voices;
  no dubbing. External TTS only for an off-screen narrator
  (`scripts/voiceover.py`).
- Before every Generate: `scripts/project_state.py can-generate <shot> --credits N`
  must exit 0; right after it: `start-take`; after QC: `log-take`.
- QC every take: `scripts/qc_clip.py` + look at the contact sheet +
  `references/qc.md`. REGENERATE always comes with the corrected prompt.
- Chrome automation: `references/platforms/google-flow/automation-kapture.md`
  — never click delete, verify settings + live price before Generate.
